// Tenants whose job heartbeat stopped, from the log.
// Backs the "no instance is polling a tenant" alert: some instance stamps each served tenant's
// heartbeat at most once a minute and logs it, so a tenant whose latest heartbeat is older than two
// minutes is not being polled anywhere: its jobs and schedules have stopped. A tenant whose poller
// retired because the tenant left the served states (frozen, suspended, retired) logs that last and
// is not reported. Tenant ids reach the log through the job machinery's log scope.
traces
| where timestamp > ago(1d)
| extend event = tostring(customDimensions["EventName"])
| extend tenant = tostring(customDimensions["TenantId"])
| where event in ("JobWorkerHeartbeat", "JobPollerRetired") and isnotempty(tenant)
| summarize arg_max(timestamp, event) by tenant
| where event == "JobWorkerHeartbeat" and timestamp < ago(2m)
